ecord for the arena Jonathan  Temari from the Philadelphia Inquirer  tweeted these photos from the rally  saying large and loud but not quite  capacity crowd as  arrived several rows open at top of  arena and some space on the floor Trump  says we have a lot of people standing  outside and he broke the all-time record  in this arena there are rows of empty  seats in here you'd think that if this  was the fullest event the arena had ever  seen it would be sold out right well  Donald Trump had the following to say  quote we really maxed out  we broke the all-time record for this  arena we broke the all-time record where  do you suppose Trump got this supposed  fact maybe out of thin air Trump could  have just said hey there's a huge crowd  here today and he would have been  correct but again this just speaks to  how regular and casual Donald Trump's  lies are becoming or really have been  all along this was happening during the  White House Correspondents Dinner the  dinner Trump refused to go to because  he's not able to take a joke because  everybody knew there was going to be  brutal comedy against Donald Trump and  rightly so this was probably Trump's  insecurity once again shining through  don't you think and in addition to  talking about crowd size he's also  starting the 20/20 rhetoric already  going back to calling Elizabeth Warren  Pocahontas so you can tell that Donald  Trump is the person that likes  campaigning much more than he does being  in office there was also a big crowd  right across the street a big protest  happening against Donald Trump endorsed  by the mayor of Harrisburg who also said  quote I hope he will look around and  understand that he needs to do more than  rally his supporters he needs to listen  to and speak with those who didn't vote  for him that's Eric Papenfuse the mayor  of Harrisburg Pennsylvania I would  suggest that mayor Papenfuse not hold  his breath lying about crowd size is  sort of like a penis size contest of  sorts when 